Recently I posted suggesting some new classes, the Dwarf, Investigator and
Jester. Dwarf has been described earlier, and I really cannot see why the flag
should be problem, you could always make the difference with upper/lowercase
(-d = dwarf, -D = debugging mode) or slightly different flags (-d/-D = de-
bugging mode, -d2 (or whatever) = dwarf, or the other way around).

Well, someone also asked for details on the Jester class. Here are some I had
in mind:

	-Begins the game with 3 cream pies, a musical instrument (n% magical),
	one or more scrolls of taming, possibly confuse monster (see later)
	but with NO decent armour or weapons
	-n% chance of getting a magic wand at the beginning of the game
	-Somehow it should be possible for the Jester to make puns to amuse
	i.e. to tame peaceful monsters/angry shopkeepers or confuse hostile
	monsters. Perhaps the musical instrument could be used for this purpose

As for the Investigator ("detective"):

	-Stealth, automatic searching
	-Magnifying glass (is there such an item in the game? Really dunno)
	and a magic marker
	-Quest: This was suggested in an email by another guy, and it sounds
	...intriguing. He said that in Call of Cthulhu the players are called
	"investigators". Thus the investigator quest might involve a city 
	called R'lyeh... You sure you want to hear more? :-)

